WEBVTT

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.630
This feels great!

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.590
Bubbles in every direction.

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:13.890
My hair's gotten so coarse.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.350
What's this?

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.390
Mariko, what's wrong?

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.360
It's going to stop.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:32.650
Don't tell me.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:09.630
The marks are the positions in which
the Musashi has been sighted.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:10.170
April 22nd 20:30

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.960
I wonder where they're heading.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:16.300
My guess is they want
to get close to the mainland.

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:20.800
The school has ordered us
to pursue the Musashi, right?

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:26.430
It seems we're the only ship they've been able
to make contact and mobilize right away.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:32.980
Maybe Ms. Minami was right and everyone
was somehow affected by that rat-like animal.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:37.450
For now, all we can do is search this area.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:41.780
Captain, I can't find anything
out of the ordinary.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.910
I thought the tank was already repaired.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:47.540
But it looks like we still have
a leak somewhere.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:51.170
I guess we'll just have to
call in for supplies, Capt...

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.250
Yeah. I agree.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.630
We'll rendezvous with a supply ship
five days from now.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.140
We'll have to conserve water until then.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.310
Coco, would you check the weather map?

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:05.310
Yes, ma'am.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:09.310
April 25th 10:40

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.310
I'm thirsty!

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.570
You should have a ramune.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.860
I'm sick of that.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:16.820
I see.

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.190
It makes you gain weight, too.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:22.450
- "That's why water is so important!"
- "Please do your part to conserve water!"

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:22.450
Is there a menu that doesn't use water?

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.910
What to do about the bathroom?

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.410
What, we can't use the toilet?

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:32.420
- Seawater is used for flushing, so...
- Oh yeah.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:36.250
After we stocked up on all that toilet paper...

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.800
CONSERVE WATER

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:42.550
Who used saltwater?!

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.930
- Come out! Who was it!
- I forgot...

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:49.430
- Did you hear about Kuro?
- Aye.

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:51.440
From Today, Use Seawater for Showers and WC

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:51.440
Yikes.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:56.190
It's been three days, though.
Should I even wash?

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.820
What's with your hair?

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:03.660
It gloriously exploded, huh?

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:09.290
But a girl's hair is her life.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.120
So sparkly.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.420
How can that be?

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.630
Don't ask me!

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.920
Boiled mackerel and tomato.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.800
Mixed vegetables and hardtack.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.850
The perfect canned goods meal, eh?

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:27.060
Beggars can't be choosers.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:29.970
Well, no sense complaining. Let's eat.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:31.940
I wish it would rain.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:34.810
I'm at my limit.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:36.940
What should we do?

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.940
I don't want my panties
to smell like salt water.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.570
- I know.
- It's gross.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:48.830
You can't take carbonation? Shiro—

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:49.950
Deputy-Captain?

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:51.580
"WATER CONSERVATION OPERATION!!"

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:55.380
U-Um, we're about to head into some fog.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.670
Ah, okay.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:02.050
Sato, please turn on the searchlight.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.720
Coco, please ring the foghorn.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:17.610
Rain!

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:57.440
I'll help, too!

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:05.740
This is no time to be collecting rain water.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:07.700
Ow!

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.990
It's slippery!

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:11.790
The water we collected...

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.120
Retreat! Retreat!

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:16.790
It's a huge low atmospheric pressure!

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:27.090
Captain, I need to talk to you.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:33.010
<i>The upper deck is currently
off limits due to the severe weather.</i>

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:36.060
<i>I repeat. The upper deck is currently
off limits due to the severe weather.</i>

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:35.930
It's inconvenient when we can't cross the top.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:40.110
So then their friend said...

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:40.110
I wonder what's for dinner tonight.
I'm hungry.

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:42.230
Go ahead.

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:43.270
Thank you.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.110
Oh, sorry!

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:51.240
Alright!

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.000
Wow.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.750
Is something wrong, Ms. Misaki?

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:04.130
Y-Yeah. I'm a little...

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:11.300
Sorry. I'm going to get someone
to cover for me!

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:20.060
Oh my gosh! She's so cool!

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:24.820
W-What are you doing to my Macchi?!

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:25.320
Captain?

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:27.570
- Okay, calm down!
- I can't calm down!

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:30.320
I'm gonna punish her
until she learns her lesson!

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.370
<i>For me, taking my life...</i>

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.790
- "is the same thing...
- as pluckin' eyebrows!"

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:39.710
- This part is great, huh?
- I couldn't agree more!

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:41.830
Why are you watching it in my room?

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:44.790
I don't have a TV in my room.

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.550
Want to watch too, Deputy-Cap?

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:47.210
No thanks.

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:49.340
Here it comes!

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:52.970
D-Deputy-Captain, I apologize
for bothering you so late.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:56.350
What is it?

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:00.730
Sorry, but would you take my watch?

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:03.230
- "What's with ya, huh?"
- "Jus' say it."

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:05.820
It's just really...

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:06.860
"Wot is?!"

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:07.980
"Jus' say it!"

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:09.610
<i>If I didn' say nothing, then I—</i>

00:08:09.610 --> 00:08:10.740
The lightning...

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:14.490
"I see it. I got it."

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:17.620
"Ain't that it. I'll go, then."

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:22.080
"I ain't takin' orders from no one."
Woosh!

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:30.380
I'd like to go to sleep.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:35.640
Are you that scared of lightning?
It's not true that it'll steal your belly button.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:38.010
It's not that I'm afraid of lightning.

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:39.350
Then what is it?

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:43.480
It just...

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:48.320
...makes me remember.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:55.320
<i>Passengers, this ship is currently
transmitting a distress beacon.</i>

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:58.410
<i>Please remain calm
and follow the crew members'</i>

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:00.080
The water's already here! Hurry up!

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:02.160
<i>instructions until
the Blue Mermaids arrive. I repeat...</i>

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:02.040
There's no time!

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:05.290
Mom, that hurts!

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:08.380
Akeno, jump into the sea.

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:09.920
Quickly.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:12.090
- Mom and Dad, what about you?
- Hurry!

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:21.930
Dad... Mom? Why aren't they here?!

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:25.350
Why?!

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:28.860
Dad!

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:31.940
Mom!

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:40.740
Maybe if I'd jumped sooner,
Mom and Dad would have... maybe...

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:43.000
<i>Captain! It's a distress beacon!</i>

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:46.330
A distress beacon from where?!

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:48.750
A shopping mall ship, the Shinbashi!

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:52.800
135-meter span, 14,000 gross tons.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:56.130
It seems they're currently
tilted port side and flooding!

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:57.840
How many on board?

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:01.470
There are 552 people on board
and they're all evacuating.

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:02.770
Any ships in the area?

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:04.520
We're the closest.

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:08.150
- Contact the Blumer main base and the school!
- Yes ma'am!

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:13.150
This is the Destroyer Harekaze,
Captain Akeno Misaki.

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:18.030
<i>This is the Shinbashi.
We're 13 miles southeast of Falalop.</i>

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:22.660
<i>We ran aground 15 minutes ago
and are stranded.</i>

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.910
The central part of the ship is stuck on the reef.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:27.250
Is anyone injured?

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:28.580
<i>Ten people are slightly wounded.</i>

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:30.130
Are you flooded?

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:32.250
<i>I believe our port side is.</i>

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.960
Are there any fires?

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:35.760
<i>I haven't heard anything yet.</i>

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:43.060
Roger. We'll arrive in about 50 minutes.
Please continue to evacuate until then, Captain.

00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:45.020
Rin, hurry!

00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:46.690
R-Roger!

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:48.940
All hands!

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:55.030
<i>A ship has run aground in the Ulithi Atoll.
We're heading there now to rescue them.</i>

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:57.070
<i>Prepare sea rescue!</i>

00:10:57.490 --> 00:11:01.320
<i>Anyone who is free from the Weapons
and Navigation departments, help prepare!</i>

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:03.950
- Oh shoot, oh shoot!
- This is scary!

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.580
This is tight!

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:11.330
- Have I gained weight?
- I might have.

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:15.340
Although the weather is fine,
the waves are high.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:16.800
The storm cleared up.

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:19.090
Looks like the low atmospheric pressure
moved west.

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:21.470
I'd say it's tipped at a 40-degree angle.

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:24.470
There's a great danger
of flipping over if it exceeds 50 degrees.

00:11:24.970 --> 00:11:26.470
This is the blueprints of the Shinbashi.

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:30.230
Shops are on the first three floors.
Residential quarters on the fourth floor.

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:32.730
The bridge is in the center.

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:37.320
<i>Are rescue preparations complete?</i>

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:39.240
We're all set, ma'am!

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:41.110
And I'll take a skipper...

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.370
<i>You intend to desert your post again, Captain?</i>

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.040
What?

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:50.790
I wonder what a captain should do
at a time like this.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:53.460
Please don't ask me.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:55.130
I'm blanking out...

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:57.420
Please stay on board, Captain.

00:11:58.010 --> 00:11:59.550
Who'll lead the rescue party?

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:02.010
I'll do it!

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:03.350
I'll go, too!

00:12:03.850 --> 00:12:06.970
Okay. I'll give instructions from here.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:15.480
Mina, myself and the three of you
from Weapons will board the ship.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:18.570
Divers, go under to assess the ship's damage.

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:23.370
Navigators and emergency personnel,
guide the people in lifeboats over to the Harekaze.

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:24.200
Yes, ma'am!

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:29.120
We did all kinds of rescue training in middle
school, but this is our first real emergency.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:30.830
I hope we don't screw up.

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:33.330
- We'll do fine.
- No problem!

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:37.630
I have bad luck, so I hope it'll be okay.

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:41.720
Read the mood...

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:44.140
Turn on the searchlights!

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:52.980
Deputy-Captain!

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:54.850
Deputy-Captain!

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:58.360
We're on site!

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:00.740
<i>The deck is full of people!</i>

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:05.030
Let the emergency personnel handle the deck.
Go inside to see if anyone's still in there.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:06.620
Begin rescue!

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:08.410
Where's our rescue?!

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:11.660
F-First we need to get a head count, right?

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:13.250
Wristbands, wristbands!

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:15.580
Aren't we supposed to see
if anyone's hurt first?

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:18.630
We should've brought the manual!

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:21.630
I'm Mashiro Munetani,
Deputy-Captain of the Harekaze.

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.630
We'll begin checking the interior.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:26.720
It looks like there are passengers
still in the residential quarters.

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:28.300
Please help them.

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:44.650
HOPPY YAKITORI

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:45.910
PUB YOSAKOI

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:50.540
The sprinklers aren't on.

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:53.040
Then the emergency system is broken?

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:54.660
Then that means...

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:56.920
...this ship is...

00:13:57.210 --> 00:14:01.920
There's a 120-meter-long crack
along the fourth compartment of the ship.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:04.800
It appears the forward
of the third compartment is submerged.

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:06.840
<i>This is Munetani!</i>

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:09.890
<i>The Shinbashi's emergency system
isn't working!</i>

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:11.180
Has something happened?

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:13.140
<i>I don't know, but...</i>

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:15.440
Pull alongside the Shinbashi! Hurry!

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.400
R-Roger!

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:20.820
Be careful of the atoll.
Get everyone inside on our deck now!

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:22.650
SHINBASHI IS THE BEST

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:23.740
Get upstairs! Hurry!

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:26.240
Crew, we're about to finish evacuating.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:28.240
Um...

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:30.870
Tamonmaru isn't with us!

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:31.870
What?

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:33.500
I looked up and he was gone!

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:35.710
Is it a young one?

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:36.540
Yes!

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:40.290
The restaurant district of the
fifth compartment hasn't been searched yet.

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:42.000
Alright, let's go!

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:45.760
Leave Tamonmaru to us! You two evacuate!

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:48.260
This way.

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:51.640
Crew and passenger evacuation is finished.

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:54.810
<i>The rescue team in the ship have also exited.</i>

00:14:54.810 --> 00:15:00.150
<i>But we received a report that Deputy-Captain
and Mina went to conduct a search in the stern!</i>

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:04.650
Apparently a small child has gone missing.

00:15:05.490 --> 00:15:07.400
I'll look over here!

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:08.950
Alright, I'll take that section!

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:12.780
Tamonmaru!

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:21.420
The young one is...

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:23.250
...a kitten?!

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:39.060
Too... dangerous.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:40.440
Beyond a disaster...

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:42.270
Captain! The Shinbashi...

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:43.150
Cut the mooring lines!

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:44.770
Move away at full speed!

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:46.940
It's splitting in half!

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:52.410
Captain! I believe the Deputy-Captain
and Mina are still inside!

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:54.530
Crap! Crap!

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.750
Look, there she is! Mina, we're here!

00:15:58.160 --> 00:15:59.960
Mina, get away!

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:01.250
I am getting away!

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:03.630
It'll be okay, so please jump off!

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:06.250
Deputy-Captain! Deputy, do you read me?!

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:07.920
Y-Yes!

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:10.180
<i>The center of the ship split!</i>

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:13.010
<i>At this rate, it'll sink! You need to escape now!</i>

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:14.260
Roger!

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:19.680
Mina was able to get away.

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:20.810
<i>And the Deputy-Captain?!</i>

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:22.900
Not confirmed yet.

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:25.150
<i>We've lost...</i>

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:27.150
<i>...contact with her.</i>

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:34.530
You're scared, huh?

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:37.160
I'm scared, too.

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:41.000
After all, I'm really unlucky...

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:47.420
But we can't stay here.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:49.670
Let's go.

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:51.050
Deputy-Captain!

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:52.550
Deputy-Captain!

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:54.340
Shiro!

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:03.310
<i>Waiting around like this is so painful.</i>

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:07.730
<i>But... I promised Shiro.</i>

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:10.110
Get blankets to the evacuees.

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:13.990
Then prepare some food
and something warm to drink!

00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:15.200
- Yes, ma'am!
- Aye!

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:20.620
Everyone's here, right?

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:22.620
What about the Navigators?

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:25.080
They went back to the ship with the evacuees.

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:27.290
Only the Deputy-Captain is left?

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:28.500
<i>Deputy-Captain...</i>

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:34.430
It's the Blue Mermaids!

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:43.230
I'm Kishima, with the Blue Mermaids'
Rapid Response Security Fleet.

00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:47.690
I'm Hikari Ogasawara, Artillery Officer
for the Harekaze and part of the rescue team!

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:49.770
Good work. Leave the rest to us.

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:51.360
There's still one student on that ship!

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:52.860
Roger!

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:55.740
One survivor in need of help!

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:07.040
Can't be helped...

00:18:12.460 --> 00:18:14.760
Are the evacuees being fed?

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:16.720
<i>Report to me if anyone is injured.</i>

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:19.050
Would you like some rice porridge?

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:21.140
We have sweet red bean soup, too.

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:32.030
It figures...

00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:33.940
I'm so unlucky...

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:39.700
Damn it!

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:42.370
How about over there?

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:43.500
I'm not getting any respon—

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:44.580
Get the hammers out!

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:48.080
Captain, contact from the rescue boat.

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:53.250
A Blue Mermaid team
is searching for the Deputy-Captain.

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:54.760
<i>Shiro!</i>

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:02.850
I'm hungry.

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:12.480
Position of the survivor confirmed!
Vicinity confirmed! No complications!

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:17.530
Can you hear us? Don't move!
Stay right where you are!

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:19.200
<i>I'm gonna get saved.</i>

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:25.290
- Deputy-Captain!
- Deputy-Captain!

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:28.710
Are you hurt?

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:29.790
I'm fine.

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:31.500
I'm glad you made it.

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:37.760
We're saved-nya! Thank goodness-nya!

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:41.010
Why are you speaking like a cat?

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:47.890
We safely rescued Tamonmaru.

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:49.810
Thank you so much.

00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:50.940
Here you go.

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:52.270
Tamonmaru.

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:58.780
Tamonmaru, you have to go.

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:01.410
He really likes you.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:05.370
Come on, Tamonmaru.

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:08.460
Um, if you don't mind...

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:10.920
Would you like to adopt him?

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:13.130
If it's not too much to ask...

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:21.050
Sorry to bother you, but please deliver this
to Yokosuka Girls' Marine High School.

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:22.550
Roger that.

00:20:22.550 --> 00:20:24.050
And this, too.

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:25.310
This is?

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:29.060
The antibody... and my report.

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:30.480
I'm home.

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:32.270
Shiro!

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:36.150
Thank goodness you're alright!

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:39.610
I was miserable
the whole time waiting for you!

00:20:39.610 --> 00:20:44.450
Shiro, I'm... I'm sorry that I put you
through this before! I'm really sorry!

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:47.790
Ms. Munetani.

00:20:58.960 --> 00:21:03.640
Is it okay to have one more cat
on board, Captain?

00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:05.430
Of course!

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:06.930
How cute!

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:08.310
Where did he come from?

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:09.680
Let me touch him!

00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:15.310
The real Blue Mermaids are so amazing.

00:21:15.730 --> 00:21:18.980
They saved me too
when I was in that shipwreck,

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:21.570
and that's what made me
want to become a Blue Mermaid.

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:26.320
But I also thought if I went aboard a ship,
I would be able to have a family.

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:29.660
<i>My mom was a Blue Mermaid!</i>

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:30.580
<i>Huh?</i>

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:34.540
<i>Mom used to say
that comrades at sea are like family!</i>

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:41.050
<i>That's why you and I will have a huge family
when we become Blue Mermaids, Mike!</i>

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:43.590
<i>So let's make a promise to each other!</i>

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:44.800
<i>Okay!</i>

00:21:45.890 --> 00:21:49.560
That's why you always say
"Comrades at sea are like family."

00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:53.180
Is Moeka the captain of the Musashi?

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:59.820
I was always with my captain,
Thea... since middle school.

00:22:01.570 --> 00:22:04.200
Now that we have an antibody for the virus,

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:05.570
I want to hurry and save them.

00:22:06.280 --> 00:22:07.070
Right!

00:22:18.960 --> 00:22:24.970
Episode 7: In a Stormy Pinch!
